Windmc clears the severity and facility fields at the start of every
message, so a message that omits Severity or Facility gets zero in those
bits. Microsoft's message compiler instead carries the last value
forward, which is what its documentation specifies for both fields:

    If no value is specified, the value used is the value last
    specified for a message definition.

So this .mc fragment, which sets the fields once and then relies on them
for the rest of the facility:

    MessageId=0x1
    Severity=Error
    Facility=Installer
    SymbolicName=PIW_E_PROGRAM_INCOMPATIBLE
    ...
    MessageId=0x2
    SymbolicName=PIW_E_FAILED_TO_INSTALL
    ...

compiles to 0xc7010001 then 0x00000002 under windmc, where mc.exe gives
0xc7010001 then 0xc7010002. Every message after the first is silently
assigned a meaningless status code.

The values live in mc_sefa_val, so preserve its severity and facility
bits across messages instead of zeroing them. The custom bit is still
reapplied from the switch on each message, and messages that do specify
Severity or Facility overwrite the relevant bits as before, so files that
name both fields on every message are unaffected.

Two adjacent divergences from mc.exe are deliberately left alone here:
the built-in Application facility is 0xfff rather than mc.exe's 0, and
the MessageId=+N counter is global rather than per facility.

This is Sourceware bug 13971, reported in 2012 and still open. The
generated parser is patched alongside its source since bison is not run
during the build; both edits preserve the line count so the #line
directives in mcparse.c stay accurate.

--- a/binutils/mcparse.c
+++ b/binutils/mcparse.c
@@ -1606,6 +1606,6 @@
 	    (yyval.ival) = 0;
-	    mc_sefa_val = (mcset_custom_bit ? 1 : 0) << 29;
+	    /* Severity and facility carry over from the last message.  */
+	    mc_sefa_val &= (0x3UL << 30) | (0xfffUL << 16);
+	    mc_sefa_val |= (mcset_custom_bit ? 1 : 0) << 29;
 	    mc_last_symbol = NULL;
-	    mc_cur_severity = NULL;
-	    mc_cur_facility = NULL;
 	  }
--- a/binutils/mcparse.y
+++ b/binutils/mcparse.y
@@ -213,6 +213,6 @@
 	    $$ = 0;
-	    mc_sefa_val = (mcset_custom_bit ? 1 : 0) << 29;
+	    /* Severity and facility carry over from the last message.  */
+	    mc_sefa_val &= (0x3UL << 30) | (0xfffUL << 16);
+	    mc_sefa_val |= (mcset_custom_bit ? 1 : 0) << 29;
 	    mc_last_symbol = NULL;
-	    mc_cur_severity = NULL;
-	    mc_cur_facility = NULL;
 	  }
